\section{Methods}
This section describes the unified methodological framework used to construct,
execute, and validate multi-domain simulations within the Codex laboratory
environment. All methods adhere to deterministic execution posture, invariant
preservation, and hardware-agnostic reproducibility.

\subsection{1. Multi-Domain Telemetry Ingestion}
Telemetry streams are ingested across five scientific domains:
\begin{itemize}
    \item astrophysical curvature fields (Axon-FP),
    \item dual-substrate GR-QFT tensors (Janus-GRQFT),
    \item proteostatic molecular conformations (Mnemosyne),
    \item neural-spatiotemporal cortical mass fields (Chronos-V),
    \item planetary atmospheric radiative flux (Stratos-Core).
\end{itemize}

All ingestion pipelines use HEALPix spatial indexing, Bayesian kinetic
imputation, and structural coordinate mapping to reconstruct missing variables
without distortion.

\subsection{2. Deterministic Numerical Solvers}
Each subsystem employs a deterministic solver stack:
\begin{itemize}
    \item bounded PDE solvers for Navier–Stokes and neural-spatiotemporal tensors,
    \item ODE solvers for proteostatic clearance dynamics,
    \item GR-QFT dual-substrate tensor solvers for curvature–granular transitions,
    \item radiative forcing solvers for atmospheric domination control.
\end{itemize}

All solvers are Total Variation Diminishing (TVD) under stochastic perturbation.

\subsection{3. Invariant Preservation Protocol}
The unified invariant set is evaluated continuously:
\[
\Phi_{\mathrm{MW}},\quad
\Xi_{\mathrm{dual}},\quad
\frac{d[\mathrm{Aggregates}]}{dt},\quad
\Delta \tau,\quad
S_{\mathrm{int}},\quad
\sum F_{\mathrm{net}},\quad
\Vert \Delta T_{\mathrm{surface}} \Vert.
\]

Each invariant must remain bounded, drift-free, and convergent under
maximum-load execution.

\subsection{4. Hardware-Agnostic Determinism}
All simulations are executed under strict determinism:
\begin{itemize}
    \item IEEE 754 floating-point compliance,
    \item deterministic PRNG seeding,
    \item memory-safety guarantees,
    \item reproducible multi-threading via Rayon,
    \item reproducible GPU compute shaders (OpenCL/CUDA).
